  "limitations": [
    "The restricted-role PostgreSQL integration test was not executed because all four database URLs, .env, and a local database runtime were absent. Migration application, function execution, forced RLS, grants, append-only triggers, same-membership behavior, concurrent convergence, receipt/audit atomicity, and query plans remain unverified at runtime for this increment.",
    "No real Shopify privacy subscription, merchant case, customer data, browser session backed by a live OIDC provider, reverse proxy, multiple API/web replicas, clock skew, response interruption after acknowledgement, secure downstream transfer, recipient acknowledgement, or downloaded-copy disposal was exercised.",
    "Browser receipt proves only that the authenticated browser had the complete bytes before acknowledging. A browser or operating-system failure after acknowledgement but before saving the file can leave receipt evidence without a durable downloaded copy.",
    "The ten-minute token expiry limits only unused browser-receipt authority. It does not revoke, expire, locate, or delete any browser, filesystem, backup, ticket, email, or merchant-controlled copy.",
    "Packages beyond 100 source records or five MiB still fail closed and require a separately reviewed export design. Canonical, legacy, cache, search, export, replica, backup, and whole-tenant privacy disposition remain incomplete."
  ],
